    {
      "id": "step_1",
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "1  Food is pushed down the oesophagus and enters the stomach at the cardia",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0.2,
        -0.12
      ],
      "height": 0.018,
      "color": "#FFE66D",
      "billboard": true,
      "visible": false
    },
    {
      "id": "step_2",
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "2  The fundus and body store it; the wall stretches from 50 ml to over a litre",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0.2,
        -0.12
      ],
      "height": 0.018,
      "color": "#FFE66D",
      "billboard": true,
      "visible": false
    },
    {
      "id": "step_3",
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "3  Acid and the enzyme pepsin start digesting protein; the rugae unfold as it fills",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0.2,
        -0.12
      ],
      "height": 0.018,
      "color": "#FFE66D",
      "billboard": true,
      "visible": false
    },
    {
      "id": "step_4",
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "4  In the antrum, waves of muscle churn it into a paste called chyme",
      "pos": [
        0,
        0.2,
        -0.12
      ],
      "height": 0.018,
      "color": "#FFE66D",
      "billboard": true,
      "visible": false
    },
    {
      "id": "step_5",
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "5  The pylorus lets a little through at a time into the duodenum",
