          "type": "note",
          "text": "A real adult stomach from anatomical scans, with the end of the oesophagus and the duodenum. Empty it holds about 50 ml and its lining lies in folds; after a meal it stretches to 1 to 1.5 litres. Cut it open to see the folds, or separate its regions."
